@page "/legal/terms"
@model LabelsMis.Web.Pages.Legal.TermsModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of use";
    var op = Model.Operator;
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <article class="col-lg-8" id="legal-terms">
        <h1 class="h3">LabelShop terms of use</h1>
        <p class="text-muted">Last updated November 11, 2026</p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. What LabelShop is</h2>
        <p>
            LabelShop is the order, production and invoicing system that @op.Name runs for its own business at
            this address. It is not offered to the public. These terms apply to everyone who signs in to it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. Who may use it</h2>
        <p>
            Accounts are created by a LabelShop administrator for people who work for @op.Name. Use only your
            own account and keep your password to yourself. Tell an administrator straight away if you think
            someone else has used your account. An administrator can change what your account may do, or close
            it, at any time.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
            Use LabelShop only for the business of @op.Name. Do not try to reach information or functions that
            your role does not include, do not take customer or company information out of LabelShop for any
            other purpose, and do not interfere with how it runs.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4" id="quickbooks">4. The QuickBooks Online connection</h2>
        <p>
            LabelShop can be connected to the QuickBooks Online company of @op.Name. Only a LabelShop user with
            the Admin or Accounting role who is also an administrator of that QuickBooks company can connect it.
            By connecting, that person confirms they are authorised to do so.
        </p>
        <p>LabelShop uses the connection only to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>read the QuickBooks company's name and the settings that affect invoices;</li>
            <li>read the customers, products and services, classes, payment terms and tax codes it needs to prepare invoices;</li>
            <li>add a customer to QuickBooks when a LabelShop user asks for it;</li>
            <li>create, update and void the invoices that LabelShop produces, and read those invoices back;</li>
            <li>ask QuickBooks to email one of those invoices to the customer, when that option is switched on.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Sign-in happens on Intuit's own pages, so LabelShop never sees a QuickBooks password. The connection
            can be ended at any time, either in LabelShop under Setup, QuickBooks, or from the Apps menu in
            QuickBooks. Invoices that are already in QuickBooks stay there.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. QuickBooks and Intuit</h2>
        <p>
            QuickBooks is a product and trademark of Intuit Inc. Using QuickBooks itself is covered by Intuit's
            own terms. LabelShop is not made, sponsored or endorsed by Intuit.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            What LabelShop holds, and what happens to it, is set out in the
            <a asp-page="/Legal/Privacy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Changes and availability</h2>
        <p>
            @op.SentenceStart may change or withdraw LabelShop, or any part of it, and may update these terms.
            The date at the top shows when they last changed. LabelShop is provided for internal use as it is,
            without a warranty of any kind to the people who use it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. Questions</h2>
        @if (op.Email is not null)
        {
            <p>
                Write to <a href="mailto:@op.Email">@op.Email</a>@(op.PostalAddress is null ? "." : $", or to {op.Name}, {op.PostalAddress}.")
            </p>
        }
        else
        {
            <p>Ask a LabelShop administrator@(op.PostalAddress is null ? "." : $", or write to {op.Name}, {op.PostalAddress}.")</p>
        }
    </article>
</div>
